<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Sackville is a university town with some of the oldest wooden homes in Southeast New Brunswick, and a surprising number of them still heat with oil. Whether yours is a century home near the Mount Allison campus, a farmhouse in Middle Sackville, or a rental near downtown, the steel tank in the basement or beside the foundation has probably been there a long time. And when the insurance renewal shows up asking exactly how old that tank is, the letter can feel heavier than it should.</p><p>Hub City Tank Co handles <a href="/oil-tank-replacement-moncton/">oil tank replacement</a> and <a href="/oil-tank-removal-moncton/">removal</a> across Sackville and the whole Tantramar area, right up to the Nova Scotia border. We're based in Moncton, an easy run down the Trans-Canada, and Sackville is a regular stop for our crews. Estimates are free and in writing, we're licensed and insured, and our emergency line answers around the clock. Call (506) 802-3471 and we'll talk it through, no pressure.</p></div></div></section>
