    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Sackville</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Sackville Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 8px;">Oil Tank Replacement</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">New certified tanks installed in a day, sized for the tight cellars and low basements you find in Sackville's older wooden homes. We haul the old tank away and make sure your heat is running before we leave.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 8px;">Oil Tank Removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Switched to a heat pump, or clearing a house before a sale? We drain, disconnect, and remove the old tank, and leave you dated paperwork that insurers, buyers, and lawyers want to see.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 8px;">Buried Oil Tank Removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Some older Sackville properties still hide an underground tank from a past heating system. We locate it, dig it out safely, and document the condition of the site.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #DCE6EF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0D2C47;margin:0 0 8px;">Emergency Leaking Tank Service</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A leaking tank can't wait, especially when a February storm is blowing in across the marsh. Call our 24/7 line at (506) 802-3471 and we'll get a crew on the road.</p>
      </div>
</div>
